{
  "_comment": "Mac native .mcp.json — paths + Redis DNS resolved for Mac. Reviewer audit 2026-05-23 caught Docker DNS (redis://redis:6379) + /opt/ paths in master .mcp.json. start-officer-mac.sh will copy this to .mcp.json on first run (and deep-merge with instance/agents/<officer>/mcp.json if drives_computer=true). MCP hygiene 2026-07-07 (audit #3a/#16/#17/#18): make restored with env-based bearer auth, linear deleted (granted to zero agents in cabinet/mcp-scope.yml), npx versions pinned, OFFICER_NAME defaults for non-officer sessions. Doctor DEAD-sweep 2026-07-07 (follow-up): vercel dereferences ${VERCEL_TOKEN} — the canonical cabinet/.env name (.env.example + vercel.sh doctrine); VERCEL_API_KEY is the PersonalSource estate name, mapped only inside probe wrappers. neon parked — see _neon_pending.",
  "_neon_pending": "neon server entry PARKED 2026-07-07 (doctor DEAD: NEON_API_KEY exists on no fleet env surface — cabinet/.env carries only NEON_CONNECTION_STRING; cf12545a already recorded 'Captain must provision a key (org-scoped recommended)', so the entry never once authenticated). polads-ceo + stephie-ceo grants in schg-locked cabinet/mcp-scope.yml STAY (reserved-for-when-wired, scaffolds pattern). RESTORE once the Captain provisions NEON_API_KEY= into cabinet/.env (600): add to mcpServers here AND in .mcp.json, same change: \"neon\": { \"type\": \"http\", \"url\": \"https://mcp.neon.tech/mcp\", \"headers\": { \"Authorization\": \"Bearer ${NEON_API_KEY}\" } } — then restart officers (caches regen at boot).",
  "mcpServers": {
    "notion": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@notionhq/notion-mcp-server"],
      "env": { "NOTION_TOKEN": "${NOTION_API_KEY}" }
    },
    "vercel": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@robinson_ai_systems/vercel-mcp"],
      "env": { "VERCEL_TOKEN": "${VERCEL_TOKEN}" }
    },
    "redis-trigger-channel": {
      "command": "bun",
      "args": ["run", "${CABINET_SOURCE_REPO}/cabinet/channels/redis-trigger-channel/index.ts"],
      "env": { "OFFICER_NAME": "${OFFICER_NAME:-captain-session}", "REDIS_URL": "redis://localhost:6379" }
    },
    "library": {
      "command": "bun",
      "args": ["run", "${CABINET_SOURCE_REPO}/cabinet/channels/library-mcp/index.ts"],
      "env": { "OFFICER_NAME": "${OFFICER_NAME:-captain-session}" }
    },
    "make": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://eu2.make.com/mcp/stateless",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer ${MAKE_MCP_TOKEN}" }
    },
    "_comment_captain_layer": "Below: Captain-layer tools (screen memory, browser hands, native Mac hands). Wired via setup-mac.sh Steps 9-12. Officer access gated by per-officer tools: allowlist in presets/work/agents/*.md — CoS sees everything; CTO/COO see playwright; others request via CoS.",
    "screenpipe": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "screenpipe-mcp@0.18.14"],
      "env": { "OFFICER_NAME": "${OFFICER_NAME:-captain-session}" }
    },
    "chrome_devtools": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "chrome-devtools-mcp@1.5.0", "--browserUrl", "http://127.0.0.1:9222"],
      "env": { "OFFICER_NAME": "${OFFICER_NAME:-captain-session}" }
    },
    "playwright": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@playwright/mcp@0.0.77"],
      "env": { "OFFICER_NAME": "${OFFICER_NAME:-captain-session}" }
    },
    "cua": {
      "command": "cua-driver",
      "args": ["mcp", "--claude-code-computer-use-compat"],
      "env": {
        "OFFICER_NAME": "${OFFICER_NAME:-captain-session}",
        "CUA_MODEL_BACKEND": "${CUA_MODEL_BACKEND:-anthropic}",
        "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}"
      }
    }
  }
}
